{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2175-04-24 18:05:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi, I’m Dr. Lee. I’ll be part of your care team. You came in with abdominal pain, nausea, vomiting, and diarrhea. Can you tell me more about what’s been going on?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2175-04-24 18:06:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes. I’ve had loose stools, like six times a day, even though I was taking Imodium. Then I tried eating a little boiled rice and threw up twice. After that, the pain started—right here in the upper middle part of my belly."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2175-04-24 18:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Okay. The pain is epigastric—above the belly button—and it’s non-radiating. Any fever, chest pain, or trouble breathing?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2175-04-24 18:08:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "No, no fever or breathing issues. Just the pain, nausea, and diarrhea. It feels kind of like the ulcer pain I’ve had before."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2175-04-24 18:10:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I see. You’ve had a lot of similar episodes, and we know your history includes gastric bypass and reversal. We did a CT scan today to check things out."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2175-04-24 18:11:20",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "What did it show? Is there an ulcer again?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2175-04-24 18:12:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "No ulcer on imaging. But the scan did show something called a gastro-gastric fistula—basically, a small connection between parts of your stomach that shouldn’t be connected. But the bariatric surgery team reviewed it and said it’s not causing an acute problem."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2175-04-24 18:14:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Oh. So that’s not why I’m hurting now?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2175-04-24 18:15:10",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Not likely. The pain might be from missing your regular stomach meds. We’ve restarted your pantoprazole, sucralfate, and ranitidine. We also gave you some IV fluids and ondansetron for nausea."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2175-04-24 18:16:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I did skip a few doses at home because I felt so sick. But I’m worried—could this be serious?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2175-04-24 18:17:50",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your labs are stable—no infection signs, no kidney or liver issues, lipase is normal. No obstruction. So no surgical emergency. We’re watching you closely."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2175-04-24 18:19:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, that helps. But the diarrhea is still scary. Is it just from the stomach issues?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2175-04-24 18:20:20",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We sent a stool test. If it comes back positive for C. diff, that could explain the diarrhea. It’s a bacterial infection that can happen after antibiotic use or in people with complex GI histories."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2175-04-24 18:21:40",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve had that before. Treated with Flagyl. Could it be back?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2175-04-24 18:22:50",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Possibly. We’ll know more tomorrow. For now, we’re holding your loperamide—Imodium—until we rule out or treat C. diff, because it can make it worse."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2175-04-25 09:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. Your stool test came back: you do have C. diff. That’s likely contributing to the diarrhea."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2175-04-25 09:16:20",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Oh no. Is it dangerous?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2175-04-25 09:17:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It can be, but we’re catching it early. We’re starting you on oral vancomycin—125 mg four times a day—for 10 days. That’s the best treatment."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2175-04-25 09:18:50",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay. And the pain? It’s still there, though a bit better."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2175-04-25 09:20:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, we think the pain is from chronic issues—possibly visceral hyperalgesia, which means your nerves are extra sensitive after all the surgeries. We’ve been giving IV morphine as needed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2175-04-25 09:21:20",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I don’t want to rely on narcotics. Last time, I was discharged without them."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2175-04-25 09:22:40",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I know. We’re trying to avoid long-term use. But for now, we’ll use oxycodone by mouth as needed for breakthrough pain, while we treat the C. diff and get your regular meds back on track."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2175-04-25 09:24:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "What about my pain clinic appointment? I had a nerve block before, but it didn’t help."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2175-04-25 09:25:20",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, we saw that. The chronic pain team will see you again soon. They might suggest other options—like biofeedback or acupuncture—as part of a long-term plan."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2175-04-25 09:26:40",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’m open to that. I just want to feel more in control."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2175-04-26 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi again. How’s the pain today? Any vomiting?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2175-04-26 10:01:10",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "No vomiting. Pain is about a 5 now, down from 8. I had a small bowl of applesauce and kept it down."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2175-04-26 10:02:20",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s great progress. We’ll keep advancing your diet slowly. Diarrhea still happening?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2175-04-26 10:03:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, but less frequent—maybe three times today. Is the vancomycin helping?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2175-04-26 10:04:40",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Likely starting to. It usually takes a few days. We’ll keep monitoring."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2175-04-27 08:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Morning. Your labs look good. White count is normal, kidney and liver tests are stable. Pain improving?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2175-04-27 08:31:20",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, about a 3-4. I had toast and tea yesterday and no issues. When can I go home?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2175-04-27 08:32:40",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "If you keep this up, probably in a day or two. We want to make sure the diarrhea is improving and you’re comfortable on oral pain meds."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2175-04-27 08:34:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And I keep taking the vancomycin at home?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2175-04-27 08:35:10",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, for 10 days total. Don’t restart Imodium until it’s done. We’ll send you home with a prescription."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2175-04-28 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re doing well. Only one loose stool last night. We’re planning to discharge you tomorrow morning."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2175-04-28 09:01:20",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s great. What about pain meds at home?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2175-04-28 09:02:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll give you a short course of oxycodone—5 mg every 6 hours as needed—for breakthrough pain. But the goal is to rely on your regular meds: pantoprazole, sucralfate, and acetaminophen."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2175-04-28 09:03:50",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my pain clinic follow-up?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2175-04-28 09:05:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It’s scheduled for next week. They’ll help with long-term strategies—non-medication options to manage the chronic pain."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2175-04-28 09:06:20",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’m glad. I don’t want to keep coming back to the hospital."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2175-04-28 09:07:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re all on the same page. Staying on your meds, eating regularly, and following up are key to avoiding this."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2175-04-29 10:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Final day. No diarrhea since last night. Pain is mild. You’re tolerating a regular diet."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2175-04-29 10:16:20",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I feel so much better. Thank you."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2175-04-29 10:17:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. We’ll go over discharge instructions: vancomycin for 10 days, no Imodium until then, take all your stomach meds daily, and follow up with pain clinic."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2175-04-29 10:18:50",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And if the pain comes back?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2175-04-29 10:20:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Use the oxycodone as needed, but call your pain doctor. If you have fever, vomiting, or severe pain, come back to the ER."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2175-04-29 10:21:20",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. No NSAIDs, right? I’m allergic."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2175-04-29 10:22:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. Stick to acetaminophen and the plan we discussed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2175-04-30 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "All set. You’re cleared to go home. Keep up the good work."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 51,
      "time": "2175-04-30 08:01:10",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you, Dr. Lee. I’ll take care of myself."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 52,
      "time": "2175-04-30 08:02:20",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re here if you need us. Take care."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 53,
      "time": "2175-04-30 08:03:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "One last thing—should I worry about that fistula?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 54,
      "time": "2175-04-30 08:04:40",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Not right now. The surgery team said it’s not causing problems. We’ll monitor it, but it’s not why you’re sick this time."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 55,
      "time": "2175-04-30 08:05:50",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, that’s a relief."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 56,
      "time": "2175-04-30 08:07:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Focus on healing from C. diff and staying on your meds. That’s the best thing you can do."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 57,
      "time": "2175-04-30 08:08:10",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. Thanks again."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 58,
      "time": "2175-04-30 08:09:20",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. Have a safe trip home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 59,
      "time": "2175-04-30 08:10:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’m ready to get back to my routine."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 60,
      "time": "2175-04-30 08:11:40",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s the goal. Stay consistent, and you’ll do well."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 61,
      "time": "2175-04-30 08:12:50",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ll make sure to take my meds every day."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 62,
      "time": "2175-04-30 08:14:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That makes a big difference. We’re proud of your progress."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 63,
      "time": "2175-04-30 08:15:10",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thanks for not giving up on me."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 64,
      "time": "2175-04-30 08:16:20",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re a team. Take care, and see you in follow-up."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 65,
      "time": "2175-04-30 08:17:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. Bye for now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 66,
      "time": "2175-04-30 08:18:40",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Goodbye. Rest well."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 67,
      "time": "2175-04-30 08:19:50",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I plan to."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2175-04-24 17:57:00",
    "admission_end": "2175-04-30 14:42:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "The patient was admitted with abdominal pain, nausea, vomiting, and diarrhea. Imaging revealed a gastro-gastric fistula, but surgery deemed it non-acute. Stool testing confirmed C. difficile infection, which was treated with oral vancomycin. Her pain was attributed to chronic visceral hyperalgesia and likely exacerbated by missed gastrointestinal medications. She improved with symptom management, restart of home PPI, H2 blocker, and sucralfate, and a short course of oxycodone for breakthrough pain. Diarrhea resolved, diet was advanced, and she was discharged home with a plan to complete vancomycin, avoid loperamide until treatment completion, and follow up with the chronic pain clinic for long-term pain management strategies.",
    "problems": [
      "Enterocolitis due to Clostridium difficile",
      "Fistula of stomach and duodenum",
      "Epigastric pain",
      "Other chronic pain",
      "Anxiety disorder, unspecified",
      "Major depressive disorder, single episode, unspecified",
      "Obesity, unspecified",
      "Body mass index [BMI] 33.0-33.9, adult",
      "Epilepsy, unspecified, not intractable, without status epilepticus",
      "Insomnia, unspecified",
      "Hyperlipidemia, unspecified",
